"Krokodilerna kommer från den antika egyptiska staden El-Maabdeh som var platsen för en av de äldsta krokodilnekropolerna i det forntida Egypten. På Nilens östra sida, uppe på en platå, låg gravplatsen som även innehöll mumier av människor. El-Maabdeh upptäcktes officiellt (?) 1873 av den italienska ",
"Two mummified crocodile cubs, one in their linen. The mummies are in an oblong glass box, the corners and edges of which are joined together with a blue textile-reinforced strip.\n\nFrom Knut Adrian Andersson’s Catalogue II\nUddevalla - Musei - Historic - Collections: E: Foreign objects\nThe Ethnographi",
"The crocodiles come from the ancient Egyptian city of El-Maabdeh which was the site of one of the oldest crocodile necropolises in ancient Egypt. On the eastern side of the Nile, on a plateau, was the burial ground, which also contained mummies of humans. El-Maabdeh was officially discovered (?) in "
